{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["If a man give to his neighbor silver or vessels to keep — in this section [Scripture] exempts the bailee from theft and loss, and in the second section it holds him liable for theft and loss. Our Rabbis explained: the first concerns an unpaid bailee, the second a paid bailee. And according to the plain sense of Scripture: the first section, in which it is written כי יתן איש אל רעהו כסף או כלים לשמר — these are movable goods, and they were given to him to guard inside his house like the rest of his possessions; therefore if they were stolen from his house he is exempt, for he guarded them as one guards his own possessions. But the second section, in which it is written כי יתן איש אל רעהו חמור או שור או שה וכל בהמה לשמור — and the nature of animals is to graze in the field, so when he deposited them with him on condition to guard them from thieves, he deposited them with him for that responsibility, and if they were stolen he is liable."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:33.621892029Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}